WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.946
You see a place for persuasion, and a place for force.

2
00:00:05.946 --> 00:00:09.811
You haven't settled where one ends and the other begins.

3
00:00:10.711 --> 00:00:13.826
On the map, you landed somewhere in the middle.

4
00:00:13.826 --> 00:00:15.253
Not the force corner.

5
00:00:15.253 --> 00:00:17.005
Not the persuasion corner.

6
00:00:17.005 --> 00:00:19.016
The line hasn't been drawn yet.

7
00:00:19.916 --> 00:00:24.166
The Principle of Human Respect doesn't split the difference.

8
00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:29.740
Coercion, theft, and violence always reduce happiness, harmony, and prosperity.

9
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.109
Whether the cause is good or bad.

10
00:00:32.109 --> 00:00:33.851
Whoever carries them out.

11
00:00:34.751 --> 00:00:38.001
Go back to the statements where you chose force.

12
00:00:39.962 --> 00:00:42.470
What kind of problem-solver would you be,

13
00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.098
if no one could be forced to do it your way?
